// psync generic profile — Syncthing ignore patterns that fit almost any folder of code.
// Chosen with ignore_profile=generic (psync writes them into <folder>/.stignore), or pulled into
// another ignore file with: #include profiles/generic
// Unrooted patterns match at any depth. (?d) lets Syncthing delete these when
// their parent directory is removed on another host.
// Rule: anything git TRACKS must sync (otherwise it shows as deleted on the other
// host). Ignoring a directory's children (dir/*) plus a leading "!" exception keeps
// such files; exceptions must come before the pattern they carve out of.

// --- Dependencies, build outputs and caches: native per host/arch, rebuilt locally
(?d)node_modules
(?d).venv
(?d)venv
(?d)__pycache__
(?d).mypy_cache
(?d).pytest_cache
(?d).ruff_cache
(?d).tox
(?d).cache
(?d).gradle
(?d).cxx
(?d).terraform
(?d).next
(?d).turbo
(?d)target
(?d)android/build
(?d)android/app/build
(?d)ios/build
(?d)ios/Pods

// --- Git: lock files must never travel, or the other host thinks git is running
.git/**.lock
.git/gc.pid

// --- SQLite companions: only meaningful to the process that has the DB open
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
